# INERT — kept only as a signpost.
#
# This file is NOT a $HOME/.gitignore. The repo is a bare git dir whose
# work-tree is $HOME, so the repository root is $HOME, not $HOME/.cfg.
# Ignore rules placed here match nothing and give false protection.
#
# The files that actually apply:
#   $HOME/.gitignore        top-level paths (pi runtime, shell secrets)
#   $HOME/.pi/.gitignore    .pi/ subtree
#   $HOME/.pi-work/.gitignore  .pi-work/ subtree
#   $HOME/.claude/.gitignore    .claude/ subtree
#
# The rules that used to live here were duplicates of $HOME/.claude/.gitignore,
# which is live and effective. The single unique entry,
# ".pi/agent/models.json", was deliberately NOT carried over: that file holds
# provider endpoints that reference credentials as $ENV_VAR and never literal
# keys, so other machines need it tracked to reproduce the setup.